  "slug": "solar-thermal-d932",
  "summary": "Numerical emitter and absorber studies and a new AM0 property database target wavelength-selective thermal radiation for energy conversion.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is wavelength-resolved control of thermal radiation, where absorption, emission and reflection set energy conversion performance. A 16-layer MgO/Si multilayer on tungsten is inverse-designed as a selective emitter for GaSb thermophotovoltaic cells, with a modeled conversion efficiency of 47.0%. A gold-carbon metasurface uses a dielectric spacer to tune gap-mode overlap with carbon, sharpening the infrared roll-off in solar-thermal absorbers. The SpaderOptics database provides reflectivity, absorptivity and emissivity for 21 materials under the AM0 solar spectrum, relevant to absorber and emitter design. The photonic Maxwell's demon proposal, which uses one-way dielectric mirrors and wavelength-converting materials in a 3D box to accumulate blackbody radiation, is less directly tied to this design thread. The new elements are inverse design of a multilayer emitter, spacer-based gap-mode tuning, and a property database under AM0 illumination. All four items are numerical or proposal-stage.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-22"
}
